WEBVTT

00:02.335 --> 00:05.635
<i>(SINGING) It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.740 --> 00:09.006
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.111 --> 00:12.377
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.582 --> 00:15.381
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.819 --> 00:18.948
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.157 --> 00:22.092
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.461 --> 00:23.860
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.963 --> 00:25.555
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.765 --> 00:31.000
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:32.273 --> 00:33.935
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

00:36.578 --> 00:39.605
<i>Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker
with a Channel Five News Special Report.</i>

00:39.716 --> 00:42.652
<i>And I'm Diane Simmons.
A flash flood warning is in effect</i>

00:42.753 --> 00:45.086
<i>as rain continues to pound Rhode Island.</i>

00:45.190 --> 00:47.317
<i>Let's go to Asian reporter Tricia Takanawa</i>

00:47.426 --> 00:49.190
<i>(IN ORIENTAL MELOD Y)
Who's gonna tell us all about the rain.</i>

00:50.970 --> 00:55.841
Tom, residents all over Quahog have been
affected by the heavy rains,

00:55.977 --> 00:58.742
although some are doing their best
to ride it out.

00:58.847 --> 01:03.615
For example, I'm here with
Rides-a-Ten-Speed-Everywhere Guy.

01:03.720 --> 01:07.122
Sir, why are you riding your ten-speed
in the rain?

01:07.224 --> 01:09.249
I don't mind.
A little drizzle never hurt anybody.

01:09.361 --> 01:12.387
I like riding the ten-speed
because it's fun, gives me energy,

01:12.497 --> 01:13.863
and it's a great way to stay in shape.

01:13.966 --> 01:16.093
How long have you lived in Quahog?

01:16.202 --> 01:18.637
Well, I used to live in the city,
but I decided moving here

01:18.739 --> 01:21.106
would be a little more relaxing,
a little more manageable,

01:21.209 --> 01:22.471
and it's a great way to stay in shape.

01:22.577 --> 01:24.273
What do you do for a living?

01:24.380 --> 01:26.940
I work in accounts receivable
at Quahog Insurance.

01:27.049 --> 01:30.918
It's not too demanding, the pay is good,
and it's a great way to stay in shape.

01:31.021 --> 01:33.991
Well, we should wrap this up.
You're getting wet.

01:34.091 --> 01:37.892
Well, I'm living life before the cancer
I have kills me, so I don't mind the rain.

01:37.996 --> 01:40.488
Water feels good on my skin.
It's cool, refreshing,

01:40.600 --> 01:43.331
- and it's a great way to stay in shape.
- What kind of cancer?

01:43.437 --> 01:46.407
It's rectal cancer. It's slowly eating
away at my lower insides.

01:46.508 --> 01:48.135
It's a quick process,
both painful and untreatable,

01:48.243 --> 01:49.233
and it's a great way to stay in shape.

01:51.202 --> 01:53.763
Thank you, Tricia. Some local residents
have even been evacuated

01:53.872 --> 01:55.999
to Quahog Stadium
for their own protection.

01:57.810 --> 02:00.746
- Why do I have to stay here?
- We just think you'll be safer.

02:00.848 --> 02:03.214
- But my house is dry.
- Here's a blanket.

02:03.317 --> 02:06.310
If you're looking for a bathroom,
it's all around you.

02:08.157 --> 02:10.022
Oh! Crap, Peter, it's a flash flood!

02:10.126 --> 02:13.221
Oh, man, I better save my autographed
picture of Dean Cain.

02:13.330 --> 02:15.731
You know, from before he got
all desperate for attention.

02:17.969 --> 02:19.699
Hey, is that Dean Cain on that park bench?

02:19.805 --> 02:21.033
Oh, God.

02:21.875 --> 02:25.276
PETER: Lois, you may wanna
come down here!

02:26.714 --> 02:27.681
(GASPS)

02:27.782 --> 02:29.774
- Oh, my God!
- I know, about the water, right?

02:29.885 --> 02:31.409
Wow, cool.

02:32.622 --> 02:34.317
- Hey, Chris, come here.
- What? Why?

02:34.423 --> 02:36.449
- Just come here.
- What is it, Dad?

02:36.560 --> 02:39.928
Does it feel like the water
suddenly just got warmer?

02:40.031 --> 02:41.225
- No.
- Oh, that's right.

02:41.332 --> 02:42.959
It's pee that makes it warmer.

02:43.067 --> 02:45.901
Peter, the water's rising fast!
We gotta get outta here!

02:46.005 --> 02:48.998
Hang on, Lois. There's a case of beer
in the fridge. I can't leave that behind.

02:49.109 --> 02:50.474
Meg, you're a good swimmer. Go get it.

02:50.577 --> 02:51.772
What? But Dad...

02:51.879 --> 02:55.509
And for God's sake, do not be afraid to
make me a sandwich while you're in there.

02:58.822 --> 03:00.084
(INHALES)

03:06.965 --> 03:08.991
Peter, Meg's been in there a long time.

03:09.101 --> 03:12.195
Boy, you cannot wait to criticize her
at every turn, can you?

03:12.305 --> 03:13.739
Go get her!

03:18.246 --> 03:20.306
Well, Lois, I am sorry
for snapping at you earlier.

03:20.416 --> 03:21.678
You were right to criticize Meg.

03:21.784 --> 03:23.650
She could not even handle
this simple task.

03:23.753 --> 03:26.051
She's in there right now,
taking a nap underwater.

03:26.156 --> 03:28.125
For God's sake, save her!

03:32.297 --> 03:35.062
My God, we better get her to a hospital.
She doesn't look too good.

03:35.168 --> 03:38.627
Yeah, she looks worse than Andy Garcia
when he had his conjoined twin.

03:39.206 --> 03:42.665
I had a great time with you tonight.
You're really amazing.

03:42.777 --> 03:45.110
Thanks, Andy. I had a great time, too.

03:45.214 --> 03:48.274
Hey. How about some love
for shoulder guy over here?

03:48.384 --> 03:51.183
- Shoulder guy wants to get in on this.
- Just ignore him.

03:51.288 --> 03:52.620
Okay.

03:52.724 --> 03:55.192
So, do you maybe want to go
in the other room?

03:55.293 --> 03:56.693
Sure. Sounds good.

03:56.795 --> 03:59.127
And shoulder guy's going with you.

03:59.231 --> 04:01.700
- Rick, shut up!
- Hey, bitch, wanna suck on my tooth?

04:05.373 --> 04:08.138
Mr. And Mrs. Griffin,
I'm afraid your coma's in a daughter.

04:08.243 --> 04:09.232
(LAUGHS)

04:09.344 --> 04:11.506
I mean your daughter's in a coma.

04:11.614 --> 04:14.607
Oh, my God, did you...
Did you hear what I said?

04:14.718 --> 04:16.185
Brain freeze!

04:16.921 --> 04:20.551
Oh, my God.
That one is going in the Christmas letter.

04:21.360 --> 04:24.956
Oh, my God, Peter.
What if she doesn't come out of it?

04:25.065 --> 04:29.560
I know, Lois. I never realized until now
how much I've taken her for granted.

04:29.671 --> 04:31.104
I mean, she's my only daughter,

04:31.205 --> 04:34.266
and I feel like I've never treated her
as well as I should have.

04:34.710 --> 04:36.178
Hey, Meg, you got something
on your shirt.

04:36.279 --> 04:37.507
(LAUGHING)

04:40.551 --> 04:41.745
Hi, Dad.

04:42.620 --> 04:46.854
Don't be too hard on yourself, Peter.
We all do things that we're not proud of.

04:46.960 --> 04:49.690
Well, I am gonna change.
You hear me, Meg?

04:49.796 --> 04:53.859
If you come out of this, I am gonna treat
you like a princess for the rest of your life.

04:53.969 --> 04:54.993
'Cause I've been a worse
father than Abraham.

04:57.400 --> 04:59.995
You wanna tell me
what the fuck that was?

05:06.464 --> 05:09.923
Excuse me, I'm Dr. Milano.
I'm the intern for this floor.

05:10.035 --> 05:12.004
You know,
you guys can probably go on home.

05:12.105 --> 05:14.437
We'll let you know if there's any change
in your daughter's condition.

05:14.540 --> 05:16.065
Wow, you're a real doctor?

05:16.176 --> 05:18.610
Hey, does Scrubs work here?
I love that guy.

05:18.712 --> 05:21.614
I wanna meet Scrubs,
and I wanna meet black Scrubs, too.

05:29.960 --> 05:33.728
Well, hello, sleepyhead. I'm Michael.

05:33.832 --> 05:35.891
Hi, Michael. I'm Meg.

05:36.001 --> 05:38.562
- Meg!
- Oh, my God, Meg, you're okay!

05:38.671 --> 05:42.301
Oh, Meg, my beautiful daughter!
Things are gonna be different.

05:42.410 --> 05:44.709
No more will I treat you
like some kind of alien.

05:45.180 --> 05:48.617
<i>WOMAN ON PA: Three minutes
to minimum safe distance.</i>

05:49.018 --> 05:54.651
Stop. Not so fast, y'all. You think you can
just up and run away, you crazy.

05:55.159 --> 05:58.994
I like to eat people from other planets.
Especially y'all.

05:59.098 --> 06:01.362
I likes to eat you with
my little mouth, too.

06:01.467 --> 06:03.959
Now, y'all get back up inside me,
little mouth.

06:04.070 --> 06:05.765
I wants to play, too.

06:05.872 --> 06:09.309
Get back inside!
I'll get you when we's eating them.

06:12.381 --> 06:15.647
- So, what is it you wanted to show me?
- That, Brian.

06:16.619 --> 06:18.178
What? It's a rundown old house.

06:18.289 --> 06:22.158
Well, yes, I suppose, to the untrained eye,
that's what it would look like.

06:22.260 --> 06:23.921
Walk inside with me, Brian.

06:26.382 --> 06:28.943
This is disgusting.
It smells, it's falling apart,

06:29.053 --> 06:30.953
and you can hear the mice
humping in the wall.

06:31.055 --> 06:32.546
(MICE MOANING)

06:35.995 --> 06:37.986
MOUSE: That was so awesome!

06:38.097 --> 06:40.123
That's why we can get it for a steal, Brian.

06:40.233 --> 06:42.360
We fix it up and sell it for a huge profit.

06:42.469 --> 06:44.961
You're crazy.
No, I'm not gonna buy this house with you.

06:45.073 --> 06:48.942
Fine. I'll just give the profits to another
investor. Plenty of others interested.

06:49.044 --> 06:51.536
- Oh, yeah? Like who?
- Mort Goldman for one.

06:51.648 --> 06:54.880
Says it's a smart investment.
But what does he know? He's only Jewish.

06:54.986 --> 06:56.248
- All right, I'm in.
- Perfect!

06:56.354 --> 06:59.347
By Christmas, you and I are
gonna be richer than Bob Saget.

06:59.725 --> 07:02.286
- So you wanna grab something to eat?
- Sure.

07:02.395 --> 07:04.261
- You ever ride in a limo?
- No.

07:04.365 --> 07:07.163
<i>Well, how about Full House
buys you a ride in a limo,</i>

07:07.267 --> 07:10.567
<i>and America 's Funniest Home Videos
buys you a shrimp cocktail?</i>

07:10.672 --> 07:11.901
Get lost.

07:12.908 --> 07:14.398
If I give you $5,000,
will you tell me I matter?

07:19.571 --> 07:23.599
Oh, there's my little angel!
Here, let me get that for you, sweetie!

07:23.709 --> 07:25.074
Thanks, Dad.

07:25.811 --> 07:27.143
Wow, Peter, I gotta say,

07:27.247 --> 07:29.876
you've really been true to your word
about treating Meg better.

07:29.984 --> 07:32.578
She's my only daughter, Lois.
She needs to be protected,

07:32.687 --> 07:36.853
like a rare gemstone or the herniated
scrotum of an older gentleman.

07:36.960 --> 07:40.556
Well, I think you've been wonderful.
Like when you took her to that new movie,

07:40.665 --> 07:43.327
<i>I'm Rich, and You're Poor,
but Let's Dance Together.</i>

07:43.768 --> 07:46.795
I'm rich, and you're poor,
but let's dance together.

07:46.905 --> 07:49.568
- Society won't like it.
- I don't care.

07:49.776 --> 07:52.007
Good for you. Good for you.

07:52.313 --> 07:55.477
Yeah, and I can't believe how you stood up
to Connie D'Amico for me.

07:56.051 --> 07:58.383
- Hey, Meg.
- Hi, Connie.

07:58.486 --> 08:00.455
I can't fit all my books in my locker.

08:00.556 --> 08:03.117
Can I put the rest of them
on your ginormous ass?

08:03.226 --> 08:04.318
(LAUGHING)

08:04.428 --> 08:06.920
Hey, Connie, hi. Peter Griffin, Meg's father.

08:07.098 --> 08:11.035
Say, can you do me a favor?
You see that fire extinguisher there?

08:12.104 --> 08:15.097
Dad, that's enough! Dad, that's enough!

08:16.944 --> 08:18.468
That's enough, Dad!

08:18.579 --> 08:19.773
(CRYING)

08:24.487 --> 08:27.548
I just want you to know, Meg,
if there's anything you ever want,

08:27.658 --> 08:31.686
- all you gotta do is ask.
- Really? Well, there kind of is one thing.

08:31.796 --> 08:32.854
(DOORBELL RINGS)

08:32.964 --> 08:34.329
(GASPS) There he is now!

08:36.102 --> 08:37.399
Hey, Meg. You ready to go?

08:37.503 --> 08:41.531
Dad, you remember Michael Milano
from the hospital. He's my date.

08:41.775 --> 08:42.800
Oh.

08:43.244 --> 08:46.806
Say, Michael, can you do me a favor?
You see that fire extinguisher there?

08:51.287 --> 08:53.779
Stay away from my daughter,
you possible rapist!

08:53.891 --> 08:56.052
Dad, stop it! Michael's my date!

08:56.160 --> 08:59.062
Meg, I almost lost you once,
I'm not gonna lose you again!

08:59.164 --> 09:00.996
This guy may look harmless
on the outside,

09:01.100 --> 09:04.400
but on the inside he could be
a complete bastard, like Fred Flintstone.

09:04.938 --> 09:07.430
So, why exactly
do you want this separation?

09:07.542 --> 09:11.240
Well, Mr. Stoneberg, in a nutshell,
the cat put me outside.

09:11.347 --> 09:14.909
I was banging on the door
for like 20 minutes, shouting, "Wilma."

09:15.018 --> 09:16.007
I didn't hear you.

09:16.119 --> 09:19.521
- There's no way you didn't hear me.
- I was in the shower.

09:19.624 --> 09:23.584
- Oh, she was in the shower.
- The elephant's trunk was on full blast.

09:23.695 --> 09:27.564
I couldn't hear you, and besides,
you're always yelling about something.

09:27.667 --> 09:30.432
How the hell am I
supposed to know when to pay attention?

09:30.538 --> 09:33.633
But when I wanna get my rocks off,
you're nowhere to be found,

09:33.742 --> 09:35.869
you passive-aggressive bitch.

09:36.278 --> 09:38.247
Meg, can I talk to you
in the kitchen, please?

09:38.748 --> 09:41.684
- Dad, what the hell?
- Lois, did you know that Meg had a date?

09:41.785 --> 09:44.880
Yes. With that nice boy from the hospital.
What's the matter?

09:44.989 --> 09:47.458
We don't know him.
Maybe he's not even a boy.

09:47.560 --> 09:49.152
Maybe he's two dwarves in an overcoat,

09:49.261 --> 09:52.356
wanting to see what sex
is like with a big person. Huh?

09:52.466 --> 09:53.524
Is that what you want?

09:53.633 --> 09:55.659
Two crafty dwarves in your house,
after your daughter?

09:55.770 --> 09:57.101
Wait. Do dwarves grant wishes?

09:57.205 --> 09:59.367
No, Peter, they're people,
like you and me.

09:59.475 --> 10:02.934
Well, goodbye phone in the bathroom,
but I still don't like Meg dating that boy!

10:03.046 --> 10:06.915
Guys that age, all they care about
is putting their thing in everything.

10:07.017 --> 10:10.351
I'm not gonna let Meg turn out
like my Nerf football in the hall closet.

10:10.455 --> 10:12.822
Dad, didn't you say
you'd give me whatever I wanted?

10:12.925 --> 10:14.688
Well, I wanna go out with Michael.

10:14.794 --> 10:18.629
Peter, you're being overprotective.
Look, why don't you just talk to him?

10:18.732 --> 10:20.792
You might find out he's not so bad.

10:20.902 --> 10:23.370
All right, Lois,
but I know what my gut tells me,

10:23.472 --> 10:25.372
and right now it's telling me I have...

10:25.474 --> 10:26.941
<i>(MAN READING)</i>

10:28.545 --> 10:31.674
But I'll suck it up and talk to Michael.
Even though I've also got...

10:31.816 --> 10:33.283
<i>(MAN READING)</i>

10:37.514 --> 10:41.281
So you are here to take out my daughter.
What are your intentions?

10:41.385 --> 10:44.753
I just think Meg is really cool,
and I want to get to know her better.

10:44.856 --> 10:47.826
You know, Michael,
my daughter's womb is not a wildfire

10:47.927 --> 10:50.488
for you to douse
with your adolescent seed.

10:50.597 --> 10:53.658
- Neither is her lower back or her hair.
- I understand.

10:53.768 --> 10:58.832
Do you, Michael? Do you? We'll see.
Let me ask you a question.

10:59.075 --> 11:01.874
You ever sit on your arm till it falls asleep
and then play with yourself

11:01.979 --> 11:03.675
and pretend like somebody
else is doing it?

11:03.781 --> 11:05.749
Honestly, yes.

11:06.117 --> 11:08.643
Not anymore you don't,
'cause you're going out with my daughter.

11:15.783 --> 11:17.512
Morning, Brian. Here, put this on.

11:17.619 --> 11:20.350
- How long have you been here?
- 7:00 a.m. All right, here's your hammer,

11:20.456 --> 11:22.357
here's your walkie,
and here's your stud-finder.

11:22.459 --> 11:23.448
(IMITATES BEEPING)

11:23.560 --> 11:27.725
Oh, well, it's working.
All right, joke time is over.

11:27.832 --> 11:29.733
Work time has begun.

11:29.835 --> 11:30.995
You get started with this drywall,

11:31.103 --> 11:33.834
and I'm gonna start pulling out
those old floorboards in the kitchen.

11:33.940 --> 11:35.932
Hey, Brian. Knock, knock.

11:36.043 --> 11:37.067
Who's there?

11:37.177 --> 11:39.338
(WHISPERING) Two friends
building a house together.

11:44.854 --> 11:49.224
Hey, Meg, I got you something
for our three-week anniversary.

11:49.359 --> 11:51.555
Wow, a Maroon 5 CD.

11:51.663 --> 11:54.565
Yeah, I remember how you told me
you liked terrible music,

11:54.667 --> 11:55.861
so I thought you might appreciate it.

11:55.968 --> 11:57.960
You're so thoughtful!

11:59.673 --> 12:01.835
- What the hell?
- What's wrong?

12:01.942 --> 12:02.909
Uh...

12:03.010 --> 12:06.970
Meg, I'm not sure, but I think your
dad is sitting at that table over there.

12:07.082 --> 12:10.382
- What? Where?
- Well, I can't tell if it's him.

12:10.486 --> 12:13.012
I think he's wearing
some kind of disguise.

12:13.123 --> 12:14.920
Oh, my God, Dad!

12:15.025 --> 12:16.516
What do you think you're doing?

12:16.628 --> 12:18.118
(IN MOCK CHINESE ACCENT)
Peter? Who Peter?

12:18.229 --> 12:21.097
I didn't say "Peter." I said "Dad."

12:21.200 --> 12:23.226
Ohhh!

12:23.337 --> 12:25.828
Have you been spying on us
the entire time we've been dating?

12:25.939 --> 12:28.500
Meg, it's only because I wanna make sure
this guy treats you right

12:28.609 --> 12:30.008
and doesn't try anything funny.

12:30.111 --> 12:32.307
Meg, this is more than I can deal with.

12:32.414 --> 12:35.407
If your father is this opposed
to our relationship,

12:35.518 --> 12:37.851
- I don't see how it can work out.
- But, Michael...

12:37.955 --> 12:40.856
I'm sorry, Meg.
I promise I won't forget you.

12:42.427 --> 12:45.556
See, look, Meg. He just walked out on you.
He's a bad man,

12:45.665 --> 12:46.996
like Jodie Foster.

12:48.435 --> 12:49.561
(DOOR SLAMS)

12:49.670 --> 12:53.004
Oh, no, Jodie. It's my husband.
He's home from work early.

12:53.108 --> 12:55.577
(IN MALE VOICE) Don't worry, baby.
He had to find out sometime.

12:55.678 --> 12:56.645
(FARTS)

12:59.216 --> 13:01.116
All right, Brian,
I'm gonna go up to the upper level

13:01.218 --> 13:02.685
and run this wire down through the wall.

13:02.787 --> 13:04.618
Grab your walkie.
I'll call you when I get up there.

13:04.722 --> 13:05.746
Okay.

13:06.692 --> 13:08.887
<i>- STEWIE: Brian, pick up. Over.
- What?</i>

13:08.994 --> 13:11.395
<i>Brian, please say '"over'"
when you finish talking. Over.</i>

13:11.498 --> 13:12.863
What? Over.

13:12.966 --> 13:14.525
<i>Do you see the wire yet? Over.</i>

13:14.635 --> 13:17.628
<i>- No.
- No what? Over.</i>

13:17.739 --> 13:18.706
No. Over.

13:18.807 --> 13:20.741
<i>Okay, I'm gonna start
feeding it through. Over.</i>

13:20.843 --> 13:24.279
Wait, if you haven't started feeding it,
why'd you ask me if I could see it?

13:24.380 --> 13:25.507
<i>Didn't copy that. Over.</i>

13:25.616 --> 13:28.745
I said, why'd you ask me if I could see it if
you haven't started feeding it?

13:28.853 --> 13:29.979
<i>- Over.
- Oh, that's better.</i>

13:30.088 --> 13:32.319
<i>I can hear you now. Over.
Do you see it yet? Over.</i>

13:32.425 --> 13:33.517
You know, you're a jackass.

13:33.626 --> 13:36.460
For the record, I don't wanna hang out
with you anymore when this is over.

13:36.563 --> 13:38.030
<i>When this is what, Brian? Over.</i>

13:38.131 --> 13:40.566
I said, I don't wanna hang out
with you anymore when this is over.

13:40.668 --> 13:43.035
<i>When this is what?
You gotta finish your sentence. Over.</i>

13:43.138 --> 13:45.834
<i>- That's it. My sentence is over.
- Your sentence is what, Brian? Over.</i>

13:45.941 --> 13:47.102
My sentence is... Wait a minute.

13:47.210 --> 13:49.770
I have to say "over," even if the sentence
ends with the word "over"?

13:49.880 --> 13:51.507
<i>Ends with the word what, Brian? Over.</i>

13:51.615 --> 13:53.948
<i>- Oh, I see the wire.
- You see the wire what? Over.</i>

13:54.052 --> 13:55.144
Over.

13:58.458 --> 14:01.451
<i>ANNOUNCER: Tonight's movie presentation
is brought to you by Sanka.</i>

14:01.562 --> 14:03.530
<i>(SINGING) Don't you wanna, wanna Sanka</i>

14:03.630 --> 14:05.565
<i>Don't you wanna, wanna Sanka</i>

14:05.667 --> 14:07.932
<i>Don't you wanna, wanna Sanka</i>

14:08.037 --> 14:11.872
<i>It doesn't keep me up at night,
but it helps me poo.</i>

14:12.876 --> 14:14.138
(SOBBING)

14:15.847 --> 14:18.611
Meg, sweetie, it's been like two weeks.

14:18.716 --> 14:20.708
Don't you think it's time
to forget about that boy?

14:20.819 --> 14:23.550
Yeah, Meg, he was a bum anyway.
You'll find another fella.

14:23.656 --> 14:25.954
I could set you up with one of my friends.

14:26.060 --> 14:28.551
Oh, wait, I don't have any friends.

14:28.662 --> 14:30.563
I could set you up with Dad.

14:30.665 --> 14:32.860
Dad, would you be interested
in dating Meg?

14:32.968 --> 14:35.733
I certainly would.
There, Meg, everything's fine.

14:35.838 --> 14:40.139
- It's not Michael I'm upset about!
- Well, what is it, then?

14:40.244 --> 14:41.906
I'm pregnant!

14:43.014 --> 14:46.974
Dad, I swear to God, I didn't know that
when I set you up with her.

14:51.759 --> 14:53.750
Oh, I can't believe this.

14:53.861 --> 14:56.695
My baby's pregnant.
How could this happen?

14:56.798 --> 14:59.324
I don't know, but regardless of
how it happened, it happened.

14:59.435 --> 15:02.496
You're pregnant, Meg,
and there's only one thing to do.

15:08.580 --> 15:11.607
Meg, can you turn over?
I gotta get that thing out of there.

15:11.717 --> 15:15.176
You're sitting on my shirt.
I gotta put it on this hanger.

15:15.289 --> 15:18.623
Now, I'm going to Michael's house
to force him to marry you.

15:20.462 --> 15:23.226
Dad, please don't do this!
You can't make him marry me!

15:23.332 --> 15:24.857
I just wanna talk to him.

15:24.968 --> 15:27.402
- Why do you have a shotgun?
- I just wanna talk to him.

15:27.504 --> 15:29.063
- Dad, this is ridiculous!
- I just wanna talk to him.

15:29.173 --> 15:30.868
- Put that gun away!
- I just wanna talk to him.

15:30.975 --> 15:32.807
Wait, what are you doing?
It is not his fault.

15:32.911 --> 15:34.344
- It was an accident!
- I just wanna shoot him.

15:34.446 --> 15:35.607
- You can't shoot him!
- I just wanna talk to him.

15:35.715 --> 15:38.013
Wait, what are you doing?

15:38.117 --> 15:41.110
- You got my Meg pregnant.
- What?

15:41.221 --> 15:44.521
Oh, my God, Meg, why didn't you tell me?

15:44.626 --> 15:47.721
- I didn't think you wanted to see me.
- But this changes everything.

15:47.830 --> 15:50.959
I wanna be there for you, Meg. I love you.

15:52.235 --> 15:56.195
- Will you marry me?
- Yes! Of course!

15:56.709 --> 15:59.200
Now, see, that's an
even more beautiful sight

15:59.311 --> 16:02.941
than 72 virgins
waiting in heaven for a suicide bomber.

16:03.650 --> 16:05.141
Here I am!

16:05.252 --> 16:07.813
<i>We're playing Magic: The Gathering.
Wanna join?</i>

16:07.923 --> 16:09.550
Osama!

16:12.729 --> 16:14.026
Um...

16:14.130 --> 16:16.292
- You know something, Brian?
- Yeah?

16:16.400 --> 16:20.633
I'm starting to think maybe we bit off
a little more than we could chew.

16:20.739 --> 16:22.571
- Yeah.
- Well, we're in it,

16:22.675 --> 16:24.370
and we're gonna finish the job.

16:24.477 --> 16:26.776
Should we get started on the upper level?

16:28.682 --> 16:31.243
- No.
- What the hell are we gonna do?

16:31.352 --> 16:33.548
We've sunk all of our money
into this place.

16:33.656 --> 16:36.922
I've got an idea. I'll be right back.

16:39.529 --> 16:42.624
So, listen,
we're gonna want to be leaving now.

16:42.733 --> 16:43.996
- Why?
- Because I just emptied

16:44.102 --> 16:47.869
a full tank of gasoline and lit a match.
We've got about five seconds.

17:10.335 --> 17:12.303
Didn't we have an electrician
in there today?

17:12.404 --> 17:14.669
He left. Pretty sure he left.

17:14.774 --> 17:16.572
Isn't that his truck?

17:18.379 --> 17:20.143
Well, by God, Brian, we're murderers.

17:20.248 --> 17:22.682
I guess this means
you'll be going to doggie hell.

17:22.784 --> 17:24.082
(LAUGHING)

17:24.187 --> 17:25.654
(DOGS YELPING)

17:31.596 --> 17:33.291
Hey, what do you guys think of this one?

17:33.398 --> 17:35.867
Meg, are you sure
you wanna go through with this?

17:35.968 --> 17:37.868
You know, there are other options.

17:37.971 --> 17:40.166
Mom, I'm not getting an abortion!

17:40.273 --> 17:45.075
Well, I'm not saying an abortion per se,
but maybe you just drink and smoke a lot.

17:45.180 --> 17:47.239
- What?
- Just don't start doing it

17:47.349 --> 17:49.409
and then chicken out
halfway through the pregnancy,

17:49.519 --> 17:51.248
because then you wind up with Chris.

17:51.354 --> 17:52.822
Well, Lois, I got the cake.

17:52.923 --> 17:55.483
Oh, and they were all out of
the bride and groom figurines,

17:55.593 --> 17:57.027
so I got the Iron Giant

17:57.129 --> 18:00.998
and a courtroom doll that kids use to
show where the molester touched them.

18:03.771 --> 18:06.069
All right, Meg,
enjoy your bachelorette party.

18:06.173 --> 18:08.540
I am outta here, 'cause I don't need to see

18:08.643 --> 18:10.578
what you crazy girls are gonna do
while I'm gone,

18:10.679 --> 18:12.146
but just remember this is a residence

18:12.248 --> 18:14.809
and should be treated as such.
And if you girls drink anything,

18:14.918 --> 18:16.818
there's recycling under
the sink in the kitchen.

18:16.920 --> 18:18.445
Okay, have fun.

18:19.757 --> 18:22.124
So, what are we supposed to do?

18:22.227 --> 18:24.286
Yeah, this doesn't seem
like much of a party.

18:24.396 --> 18:25.364
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

18:27.033 --> 18:30.970
Hey, what's with all the noise?
Got some complaints from next door.

18:31.071 --> 18:34.371
I might have to take you girls downtown.

18:34.743 --> 18:36.507
<i>(CLUB MUSIC PLA YING)</i>

18:41.985 --> 18:44.454
Which one of you is the lucky bride?

18:46.024 --> 18:47.185
What's your name, sweetie?

18:47.293 --> 18:48.260
Dad, you know my name.

18:48.360 --> 18:49.349
(EX CLAIMS)

18:49.461 --> 18:54.526
It's Officer Nasty. Careful,
I might be carrying a concealed weapon.

19:06.517 --> 19:08.246
- Hello.
- Hi. Name, please?

19:08.352 --> 19:09.411
Neil Goldman.

19:09.521 --> 19:12.150
Goldman, Goldman.
Sorry, no Neil Goldman.

19:12.258 --> 19:15.352
Oh, I beg your pardon,
I meant to say Chris Griffin.

19:15.461 --> 19:16.793
Griffin, Griffin.

19:16.897 --> 19:19.229
Here it is.
Says you're supposed to be an usher.

19:19.334 --> 19:21.199
- Well, you'll need this.
- Name, please?

19:21.302 --> 19:24.067
- Chris Griffin.
- Griffin, Griffin.

19:24.173 --> 19:26.539
I'm sorry, sir.
Chris Griffin has already checked in.

19:26.643 --> 19:28.440
Well, that's impossible!

19:28.745 --> 19:30.213
(SOBBING)

19:30.314 --> 19:31.975
Meg, are you ready?

19:32.083 --> 19:33.915
Sweetie, what's wrong?

19:34.019 --> 19:39.424
- Mom, I can't do it. I can't get married.
- What? Well, why not?

19:39.525 --> 19:42.256
Because I'm not pregnant.

19:42.363 --> 19:44.764
What do you mean? How do you know?

19:44.866 --> 19:45.924
(SIGHS)

19:46.034 --> 19:47.296
I got my period.

19:47.402 --> 19:48.392
Oh.

19:48.504 --> 19:51.302
I must've read the test wrong.
What am I gonna do?

19:51.407 --> 19:53.069
Michael's out there waiting for me.

19:53.176 --> 19:55.702
Well, Meg,
the best thing you can do is be honest.

19:55.813 --> 19:57.474
Just tell Michael the truth.

19:57.582 --> 19:59.881
If he cares about you, he'll understand.

19:59.985 --> 20:03.649
I'll try. Thanks, Mom. I love you.

20:03.757 --> 20:05.884
I... You, too, honey.

20:06.092 --> 20:08.323
<i>(WEDDING MARCH PLAYING)</i>

20:16.739 --> 20:20.107
God, look at Meg's fat shoulders
in those spaghetti straps.

20:20.210 --> 20:22.441
It's like bread baking around twine.

20:25.151 --> 20:28.747
- Meg, you look beautiful.
- Thank you, Michael.

20:28.855 --> 20:32.451
I have never been more in love with
someone than I am with you right now.

20:32.560 --> 20:34.551
Oh, Michael, I love you, too.

20:34.662 --> 20:38.326
And I have some wonderful news.
I'm not pregnant.

20:38.434 --> 20:39.595
BOTH: What?

20:40.937 --> 20:41.904
(DOOR SLAMS)

20:44.209 --> 20:47.008
Dad, I'm sorry about this whole mess.

20:47.113 --> 20:49.981
You know what, Meg? It's all my fault.

20:50.084 --> 20:52.780
I never should have
dragged you into this anyway.

20:52.886 --> 20:56.880
I guess sometimes a father just gets
a little overprotective of his daughter,

20:56.991 --> 21:00.223
but you gotta know
I was only thinking about your happiness.

21:00.329 --> 21:02.525
I know, Dad, and I appreciate it.

21:02.632 --> 21:06.034
The problem now is that
these people are expecting a show.

21:06.137 --> 21:08.868
Ladies and gentlemen, Mr. Conway Twitty.

21:08.974 --> 21:10.407
<i>(APPLAUDING)</i>

21:10.509 --> 21:12.978
<i>(SINGING) Hello, darling</i>

21:13.079 --> 21:15.172
<i>Nice to see you</i>

21:15.316 --> 21:19.253
<i>It's been a long time</i>

21:19.354 --> 21:25.316
<i>You're just as lovely as you used to be</i>

21:28.832 --> 21:30.994
<i>How's your new love?</i>

21:31.102 --> 21:33.127
<i>Are you happy?</i>

21:33.238 --> 21:37.176
<i>Hope you're doing fine</i>

21:37.277 --> 21:44.208
<i>Just to know it means so much to me</i>

21:44.209 --> 22:45.209
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru